course: dictionary
lesson: 6747
title: Online: a word for the internet
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Online means connected to the internet, or done on it. As an adjective it describes a noun: «online games» are games you play on the internet. As an adverb it tells how something is done: «We shop online» means we buy things on the internet.
explain: Use the words around it to check. «Scary predictions online are usually nonsense meant to get attention.» Online tells you where the predictions are: on the internet. Swap in your meaning, "scary predictions on the internet", and the sentence still makes sense, so you have it right.
explain: Online also belongs to staying safe. «People online may not be who they say they are.» Keep your name, school, address and passwords private, and tell a trusted adult if something online upsets you, because not everything online is true.
fact: Online means connected to the internet, or done on it.
fact: As an adjective, online describes a noun, as in «online games».
fact: As an adverb, online tells how, as in «We shop online», meaning on the internet.
fact: Online is used at school too, for online learning and research.
fact: Keep personal information private online: your name, school, address and passwords.
exercise: «Play online only with people your family knows about.» What kind of word is online here? | Adjective, because it names a thing | Verb, because it is an action | Noun, because it is a place | *Adverb, because it tells where you play
exercise: «Online games» are popular with children. What does online mean in this phrase? | *Connected to the internet | Sad or tired | Made of wool | Very old and worn
exercise: «We shop online.» What does online mean here? | *On the internet | With our friends | Very quickly | In a shop
test: Which is a safe thing to do online? | Meet someone you only know online | *Keep your password private | Click on every free gem offer | Share your home address with a stranger
test: «Many online photos are filtered or edited.» What does this suggest? | Only grown-ups post photos online | *Some pictures are changed, so they may not look real | Every photo online is a true picture of the person | Photos cannot be changed once they are online
exam: «A girl in Ohio downloaded a cheat for an online game from a site that promised free gems; it put a virus on the family computer.» What should she have done? | Ignored the warning and kept the cheat | Shared it with all her friends | Downloaded it quickly, because free gems are good | *Asked a trusted adult before downloading anything
